---
description: Security and privacy rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- Treat URLs, HTTP headers, filenames, browser messages, and downloaded content as untrusted.
- Validate redirect targets and restrict supported schemes for ordinary downloads to http/https in MVP.
- Prevent path traversal and writes outside the chosen destination.
- Use parameterized SQL.
- Never disable TLS certificate verification.
- Do not log cookies, authorization headers, passwords, or signed URL query strings.
- Do not collect browser history or page content by default.
- Keep Wails/desktop privileges and extension permissions minimal.
- Reject malformed or oversized native messaging payloads.
- Network Access / Tunneling features require explicit opt-in, user-configurable endpoints, and a documented threat model before implementation.
